<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10239" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-gĕmo</span></b> , ŭi,
		3, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr., to sigh</i> or <i>groan
			deeply</i> or <i>loudly, to heave a sigh</i>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Prop. (rare but
			class.): congemuit senatus frequens, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Mur.
				25, 51</span></i>; * <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Tib. 23</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <b>poet.</b>, of
			trees cut down: supremum congemuit, * <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 2,
				631</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act., to deplore, lament, bewail</i>: quid mortem
			congemis ac fles? * <i><span class="en">Lucr. 3, 934</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">positum feretro congemuere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 5, 12</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
